# Duet: An Original Round (repertoire plan: st-duet-round). An original 8-bar round in G major
# for two guitars, first position on strings 4-1. The tune is four 2-bar segments, each a bar
# over G and a bar over D, so any two of them fit together:
#   1. quarters, a little turn: B C B G | A B A F#
#   2. long notes, up high: D G | F#
#   3. running eighths around B and A
#   4. the bell: G D | D F#, which leads back to the start.
# On beats 1 and 3 the two voices always sound a third, a sixth or a fifth apart, and every note
# there belongs to the chord of its bar; the other notes step between chord notes.
# You play the first voice, twice through, then two long notes while the teacher finishes, and
# the last G. The teacher starts the same tune two bars after you.
title: Duet: An Original Round
id: st-duet-round
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original round for two guitars
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: duet, round, two parts, g major, eighth notes
tempo: 84
time: 4/4
key: G

